  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Between Conventional and Experimental (2024), published by Leuven University Press, has been cited 1 time. Beyond that, it has been downloaded 1,472 times.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Between Conventional and Experimental by Regine Hess, Inbal Ben-Asher Gitler, Tzafrir Fainholtz and others was published by Leuven University Press in 2024. Conceptually, the work connects to Prefabrication, Exhibition, Architecture, Architectural engineering and Context (archaeology).</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">OpenAlex records 1 citation. Notable citing venues include Architecture Structures and Construction. The citing authors are based in the United States.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">It has been downloaded 1,472 times via OAPEN. Its subject matter aligns with Sustainable cities and communities among the Sustainable Development Goals. The work was funded by KU Leuven, Sapir College and Technion - Israel Institute of Technology.</p>",
